<!-- ACT IV: BENCHMARKS & DINER RECEIPT -->
<section class="bench-wrapper" id="benchmarks">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-head">
      <span class="kicker">Benchmarks</span>
      <h2>Measured, not promised.</h2>
      <p>
        Every bar has a command behind it, and the command is in the repository. One machine, named: an Intel i7-8750H
        laptop, <span class="mono">rustc 1.98.1</span>, no pinning, other load present. Read the ratios, and re-run the
        commands for absolute times. The commands live in
        <a href="https://github.com/bite-gpui/gpui_parley" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">
          <span class="mono">bite-gpui/gpui_parley</span>
        </a>
        , and the run is recorded in its <span class="mono">benchmarks/</span> directory.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="bench-grid">
      <div class="bench-card">
        <div class="bench-metric">
          <div class="metric-header">
            <span class="metric-title">Raster size, rounded to a lattice</span>
            <span class="metric-sub">3.3 ms a frame &rarr; 41.1 µs a frame</span>
          </div>
          <div class="bar-track">
            <div class="bar-fill before"></div>
          </div>
          <div class="bar-track">
            <div class="bar-fill after" style="--w-target: 1.2%;"></div>
          </div>
          <p class="metric-note">
            80× · a transform that asks for a different font size on every line, 30 lines a frame. The atlas stops
            missing: 154 misses a frame → 0, in 644 entries instead of 32,508. The step size is a smoothing knob rather
            than a speed one — every step costs the same ~43 µs.{" "}
            <span class="cmd">cargo run --release --example raster_cost</span>
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="bench-metric">
          <div class="metric-header">
            <span class="metric-title">Hinting instances a frame builds</span>
            <span class="metric-sub">3,480 &rarr; 30</span>
          </div>
          <div class="bar-track">
            <div class="bar-fill before"></div>
          </div>
          <div class="bar-track">
            <div class="bar-fill after" style="--w-target: 0.9%;"></div>
          </div>
          <p class="metric-note">
            116× fewer · an instance is a face's hinting program run at a size, and one costs ~31 µs. A frame asks for
            one size per line, so a cache keyed on face and size builds thirty where one instance per glyph would build
            three thousand four hundred and eighty. <span class="cmd">cargo run --release --example raster_cost</span>
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="bench-metric">
          <div class="metric-header">
            <span class="metric-title">Text as triangles instead of rasters</span>
            <span class="metric-sub">26.7 ms a screenful &rarr; 0.69 ms</span>
          </div>
          <div class="bar-track">
            <div class="bar-fill before"></div>
          </div>
          <div class="bar-track">
            <div class="bar-fill after" style="--w-target: 2.6%;"></div>
          </div>
          <p class="metric-note">
            39× the CPU per screenful · each glyph's outline is tessellated once and the same triangles are placed every
            frame: 639 µs once, then 48 µs a frame to position 3,480 glyphs as 218,322 vertices. What it costs is
            traffic, not time — see the receipt. <span class="cmd">cargo run --release --example vector_cost</span>
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Diner Receipt Card -->
      <aside class="receipt" aria-label="Performance summary receipt">
        <div class="receipt-header">
          <h3>THE DINER RECEIPT</h3>
          <p style="font-size:0.75rem; color:#64748B;">Order #0042 · Table 6 · Modular GPUI</p>
        </div>
        <div class="receipt-line">
          <span>Raster lattice, a frame</span>
          <span>80&times; FASTER</span>
        </div>
        <div class="receipt-line">
          <span>Hinting instances, a frame</span>
          <span>3,480 &rarr; 30</span>
        </div>
        <div class="receipt-line">
          <span>Text as triangles, CPU</span>
          <span>39&times; FASTER</span>
        </div>
        <div class="receipt-line">
          <span>Outline tessellation, a lookup</span>
          <span>3.8 µs</span>
        </div>
        <div class="receipt-line">
          <span>Vertex traffic, a frame</span>
          <span>42.6 MB</span>
        </div>
        <div class="receipt-line total">
          <span>THE VECTOR ROUTE</span>
          <span>3.8 ms of a 16.7 ms frame</span>
        </div>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<script>
  (() => {
    const benchIO = new IntersectionObserver(
      (entries) => {
        entries.forEach((entry) => {
          if (!entry.isIntersecting) return;
          const fills = entry.target.querySelectorAll(".bar-fill");
          fills.forEach((fill, i) => {
            setTimeout(() => fill.classList.add("is-in"), i * 110);
          });
          benchIO.unobserve(entry.target);
        });
      },
      { threshold: 0.4 },
    );

    document.querySelectorAll(".bench-metric").forEach((m) => benchIO.observe(m));
  })();
</script>
